4 MINORIA MINING IN 2D
In this section, we start by studying the problem in R2– referred to
as the 2D case. Before providing the technical details, we would like
to clarify that in the 2D case, Dcan have more than two observation
attributes (used for prediction). However, the projection directions
are considered with respect to a pair of observation attributes called
attributes of interest. For example, in our experiments in § 7, we
uselongitude and latitude as the attributes of interest for Minoria
mining in a crime dataset.
Recall that our goal is to find a set of high-skew directions. Let
H={d(𝑡𝑖)|𝑡𝑖∈D} be the set of dual hyper-planes in the dual
